{"clips": [
  {
    "id": "C1",
    "weakest_point": "The middle section becomes a repetitive, talky back-and-forth ('You don't even know me' / 'Because I know what I see') that delays the ring offer; a scroller may swipe away before the vow at 53 s.",
    "hook": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "The cruel line 'You have finally found a man as worthless as everyone thinks you are' lands at 1.5 s with no context needed, and the immediate cut to Juliana's hurt face confirms the sting. It is not a physical slap, but it is a sharp, humiliating insult that stops the scroll."
    },
    "cliffhanger": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "It ends on the line 'It is a vow,' which leaves the question of whether Juliana will accept open, but the romantic tension has already built and eased into a declaration; it is not an urgent, danger-filled peak."
    },
    "questions": [
      {
        "q": "Who is the scarred man offering the ring?",
        "type": "intrigue"
      },
      {
        "q": "Will Juliana accept his vow?",
        "type": "intrigue"
      }
    ],
    "standalone": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "With zero context you can follow that Juliana is being publicly humiliated by her family and a stranger offers her dignity instead of pity; the man's exact identity is a mystery, but his role as rescuer is clear."
    },
    "emotion": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "You feel the sharp injustice of the insult and the family's cruelty, then a swell of hope as the stranger validates her; the tear on her cheek and the vow create a strong emotional swing."
    },
    "want_next": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "You want to know if she takes the ring and who he really is, but the long, talky middle makes the payoff feel distant."
    },
    "ad_policy": {
      "level": "none",
      "category": "none",
      "reason": "Arguments, insults, and a ring offer; no physical violence, blood, sexual content, or gore."
    },
    "one_line_verdict": "A cruel insult hook and a vow ending carry it, but the talky middle tests patience."
  },
  {
    "id": "C2",
    "weakest_point": "The hook line is split by the 3-second mark and needs its second half to land; the cut to the courtyard restarts the conflict as more verbal disowning, and the final line is a resolved verdict rather than a peak.",
    "hook": {
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "Above the 3 s line we only get 'I would rather choose my own life...' which is defiant but incomplete; the stronger beat ('...than spend another moment begging for yours') arrives just after the cutoff."
    },
    "cliffhanger": {
      "score": 2,
      "reason": "The final line 'you are dead to the Ashcroft family' is a definitive verdict that has already fallen; the scene is resolved rather than cut at an unresolved peak."
    },
    "questions": [
      {
        "q": "Will Juliana survive being disowned with no dowry?",
        "type": "intrigue"
      },
      {
        "q": "Who is the soldier she chose?",
        "type": "intrigue"
      }
    ],
    "standalone": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "It is fully clear who is wronged (Juliana), by whom (her family), and what is at stake (her name, dowry, and inheritance); the only gap is the stranger's identity, which does not block the story."
    },
    "emotion": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "Righteous defiance, shocked recoil, and the cruelty of disownment create a strong sense of injustice and stakes."
    },
    "want_next": {
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "The total severing of family ties raises a clear survival question: how will she live, and who is this man who took her in?"
    },
    "ad_policy": {
      "level": "none",
      "category": "none",
      "reason": "Verbal confrontation, disowning, and walking away; no physical violence or prohibited content."
    },
    "one_line_verdict": "Clear stakes and strong family cruelty, but the delayed hook and resolved ending blunt the scroll-stop power."
  },
  {
    "id": "C3",
    "weakest_point": "It opens mid-argument on 'charity' with no setup, and it ends on the completed ring exchange, which resolves the tension entirely rather than cutting at a peak.",
    "hook": {
      "score": 2,
      "reason": "The first 3 s show a tear and the defensive line 'I will not become anyone's charity,' but without context it is unclear who is offering what or why; it needs setup to land."
    },
    "cliffhanger": {
      "score": 1,
      "reason": "The ring sliding onto her finger completes the marriage; the moment is peacefully resolved with no open question."
    },
    "questions": [
      {
        "q": "Why does Juliana think his offer is charity?",
        "type": "confusion"
      },
      {
        "q": "Who is the bearded man?",
        "type": "confusion"
      }
    ],
    "standalone": {
      "score": 2,
      "reason": "Confusing without context: the 'charity' conflict is unexplained, the family is present but their grievance is not shown, and her sudden acceptance lacks a clear turning point."
    },
    "emotion": {
      "score": 2,
      "reason": "There is some tenderness and defiance, but the lack of setup blunts the impact; you watch a wedding rather than feel a injustice or a threat."
    },
    "want_next": {
      "score": 2,
      "reason": "Because the wedding is already proceeding and the ring is placed, the urgency to see the next episode is low."
    },
    "ad_policy": {
      "level": "none",
      "category": "none",
      "reason": "Romantic ceremony and dialogue; no violence, sexual content, or gore."
    },
    "one_line_verdict": "Starts too deep in the conversation and ends after the wedding peak; weakest standalone."
  }
],
  "best": "C1",
  "best_why": "It has the only hook that lands a cruel, context-free blow in the first three seconds, and it cuts on an unanswered vow rather than a resolved verdict."
}
